  {
   "title": "M-VAVE SMC-Mixer user manual",
   "url": "https://www.m-vave.com/download.html",
   "note": "manufacturer manual: SHIFT + ◁ / ▷ switches DAW / user mode; in DAW mode M, S, R and □ are mute, solo, record and select, and the light bar under each encoder blinks while a fader does not match the track volume"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "In DAW (Mackie) mode, which SHIFT + ◁ selects (SHIFT + ▷ goes back to user mode). Imported from QLC+'s community profile (Apache-2.0, see NOTICE); the layout follows the unit. A unit (firmware V012) was checked on 23 and 24 Nov 2026 (issue #7); the controls stay marked unverified only because files imported from QLC+ never carry hardware checks. Every message matched, with two corrections: the eight encoders are relative (sign bit: 1 = clockwise, 65 = counter-clockwise), not buttons, and the 32 strip buttons and Play, Stop, Record, Rewind and Forward light up with a Note On on the same note sent back to the unit (velocity > 0 on, 0 off; there is no blink). Bank −/+ and the arrows have no controllable light. The light bar under each encoder is not a ring: it does not answer the Mackie ring CCs 48–55; it is the unit's own soft-takeover indicator and blinks while a fixed Pitch Bend value sent to a fader differs from where the fader is. Faders have no motor and send Pitch Bend from −8192 to +8064 in steps of 128; the unit does not report their position until they move. The unit opens two input ports that repeat the same messages (\"SMC-Mixer\" and \"MIDIIN2 (SMC-Mixer)\"); the pattern picks the first. In user mode (as shipped) the messages are different: faders CC 0–7 on channel 1, encoders CC 0–7 on channel 3 (absolute), and the buttons switch their own lights.",
 "face": {
